# Audit — copy to docs/AUDIT.md and customize for your project.

When you ask for **an audit**, that means **everything** — one pass, closed scope. Report **only Fix and Improve**.

Pair with **`docs/AUDIT.config.json`** (from `AUDIT.config.json.template`).

**Reference implementation:** BSOD Analyzer `app/docs/AUDIT.md` + `app/docs/AUDIT.config.json` (also `pack/templates/docs/AUDIT.bsod.reference.md`).

## Coverage contract

- No partial audits, Phase A/B, or "extend coverage later"
- **One audit, three steps** — never `-SkipTests` for step 1
- Domain map gaps → **Fix** (auto-detected by `run_audit_core.ps1`)
- Audit file drift → **Fix** (auto-detected by `sync-audit-system.ps1 -VerifyOnly`)

## How to run

```bat
run_audit.cmd
scripts\verify_semantic_audit.cmd
scripts\finalize_audit.cmd
```

| Step | Command | Who |
|------|---------|-----|
| 1 — Machine | `run_audit.cmd` | Tooling (full tests) |
| 2 — Semantic | Edit `docs/.audit_semantic_report.json` + `verify_semantic_audit.cmd` | Auditor |
| 3 — Finalize | `scripts\finalize_audit.cmd` | Tooling (no retest when manifest proof valid) |

Re-run **full `run_audit.cmd`** only if git HEAD or source tree changed since step 1 (no-git repos use a tree fingerprint — re-run step 1 when source changed).

## Checklist sections

Define sections A–N (or your own letters) below. Include a **## Domain map** table mapping every production module to a section.

## Report format

**Fix** and **Improve** only. If none: **Nothing found.**

## After an audit

Fix items, then re-run step 1 if tests need refreshing; otherwise update semantic report and **`finalize_audit.cmd`**.

